-- title:
--   Pullback of 𝒪(± nZ) along an isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $X$, $Y$, $T$ be schemes, let $f \colon Y \to X$ be an isomorphism, let $p \colon T \to X$ be a closed immersion, and let $p' \colon T \to Y$ satisfy that $p'$ followed by $f$ equals $p$. Assume that the kernel ideal sheaf data `p.ker` is invertible and that `p'.ker` is invertible, invertibility of an ideal sheaf datum $I$ on a scheme $Z$ meaning that every point of $Z$ lies in some basic open $Z_f$ with $f \in \Gamma(Z, U)$ for an affine open $U$, such that on the affine basic open determined by $f$ the ideal of $I$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor. Then for every natural number $n$ both of the following types of isomorphisms are nonempty: first, the pullback along $f$ of the dual module $(\mathcal I_p^{\,n})^{\vee}$, that is the internal hom from the module of $p.\mathrm{ker}^{\,n}$ into the unit object of $X$-modules, is isomorphic to the corresponding dual module of $p'.\mathrm{ker}^{\,n}$; and second, the pullback along $f$ of the module of $p.\mathrm{ker}^{\,n}$ — the kernel of the unit map of $\mathcal O_X$-modules into the pushforward along the closed subscheme inclusion of the unit — is isomorphic to the module of $p'.\mathrm{ker}^{\,n}$. Only nonemptiness is asserted; no particular isomorphism is named.
--
--   This is the statement that the line bundles $\mathcal O(\pm nZ)$ attached to a closed subscheme with invertible ideal sheaf are transported by an isomorphism of ambient schemes, in the form needed for divisors supported at a point of a curve. It is used throughout the construction of the relative Picard functor and the Abel–Jacobi map, where identifications of $\mathcal O(\pm nZ)$ under isomorphisms of the base curve have to be produced.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_Hom_nonempty_pullback_ker_pow_invModule_iso_of_isIso.lean

